<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Red Army Is the Strongest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>; first printed <a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Красная Армия всех сильней, Krasnaya Armiya vsekh silney</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> Is the Strongest&quot;, widely known by its opening words as &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White Army</a>, Black Baron&quot;, is a Soviet march with words by Pavel Gorinshtein and music by Samuel Pokrass. It was written in 1920, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>, as a combat anthem for the Red Army.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>The Red Army Is the Strongest</b>&quot;, widely known by its opening words as &quot;White Army, Black Baron&quot;, is a Soviet march with words by Pavel Gorinshtein and music by Samuel Pokrass.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-red-army-is-the-strongest">The Red Army Is the Strongest</a></li></ul></section>
